UI/UX Design – Important Viva Questions and Answers
Here are simple, exam-ready questions and answers for your UI/UX Design practicals (Practical 6 to 10).
1. Basic UI/UX Questions
Q1. What is UI?

UI stands for User Interface. It is the visual part of an application, such as buttons, colors, images, text and menus.

Q2. What is UX?

UX stands for User Experience. It describes how easily and comfortably a user can use an application.

Q3. What is the difference between UI and UX?
- UI focuses on the appearance of an application.
- UX focuses on the user's overall experience.
Q4. What is Figma?

Figma is an online design tool used to create user interfaces, wireframes and prototypes.

Q5. What is a wireframe?

A wireframe is a basic layout or blueprint of an application or website.

Q6. What is a prototype?

A prototype is an interactive model of an application that shows how users can navigate between screens.

Q7. What is a mockup?

A mockup is a visual representation of the final design of an application.

Q8. What is usability?

Usability means how easily users can understand and use an application.

Q9. What is typography?

Typography is the style and appearance of text, including font, size and spacing.

Q10. What is responsive design?

Responsive design means a website or application adjusts to different screen sizes.

2. Practical 6 – User Persona
Q1. What is a user persona?

A user persona is a fictional representation of a target user based on user research.

Q2. Why do we create a user persona?

To understand users' needs, goals, interests and problems.

Q3. What are the main elements of a user persona?
- Name and age
- Occupation
- Goals
- Needs
- Interests
- Challenges
- Behaviour
Q4. What are user goals?

User goals are the things users want to achieve using a product.

Q5. What are pain points?

Pain points are the problems or difficulties faced by users.

Q6. What is empathy in UI/UX?

Empathy means understanding users' feelings, needs and difficulties.

Q7. Which tools are used to create user personas?

Figma, FigJam, Canva and Miro.
3. Practical 7 – Online Learning Platform Wireframe
Q1. What is an e-learning platform?

An e-learning platform is an online system used to learn through courses, videos and quizzes.

Q2. What is the purpose of a wireframe?

To plan the layout and structure of an application before final designing.

Q3. Which screens are included in your e-learning platform?
1. Home
2. Course Listing
3. Course Details
4. Video Lecture
5. Quiz
6. Progress Tracking
Q4. What is navigation?

Navigation helps users move from one screen or page to another.

Q5. What is a dashboard?

A dashboard displays important information such as courses, progress and activities.

Q6. What is a low-fidelity wireframe?

It is a simple design made using basic shapes, boxes and text without detailed styling.
4. Practical 8 – Social Fitness Application
Q1. What is a social fitness application?

It is an application that helps users track fitness activities and connect with friends.

Q2. What are the main features of a fitness application?
- Workout tracking
- Daily steps
- Fitness goals
- Progress monitoring
- Friends and challenges
Q3. What is workout tracking?

It means recording physical activities such as running, walking and cycling.

Q4. What is a fitness goal?

A fitness goal is a target set by a user, such as walking 10,000 steps daily.

Q5. Why are social features useful?

They help users connect, share progress and motivate each other.

Q6. What is a leaderboard?

A leaderboard displays users' rankings based on their performance.
5. Practical 9 – Product Packaging / Poster Mockup
Q1. What is product packaging?

Product packaging is the material or design used to cover and present a product.

Q2. What is a mockup?

A mockup shows how a design may look in a real-world situation.

Q3. What are the main elements of product packaging?
- Product name
- Logo
- Brand name
- Product image or illustration
- Product information
- Colors
Q4. What is a poster?

A poster is a visual design used to communicate information or advertise something.

Q5. Why are colors important in packaging?

Colors attract customers and help communicate the product's identity.

Q6. Which tools are used for creating mockups?

Canva, Figma, Photoshop and Illustrator.
6. Practical 10 – Recipe Finder Application
Q1. What is a recipe finder application?

It is an application that helps users find recipes based on ingredients, food categories or dietary preferences.

Q2. What are the main features of a recipe finder app?
- Search recipes
- Filter by ingredients
- Food categories
- Recipe details
- Cooking instructions
- Favourite recipes
Q3. What is a search bar?

A search bar allows users to find information by entering keywords.

Q4. What is a filter?

A filter helps users find specific results based on selected conditions.

Q5. What is a favourite feature?

It allows users to save their preferred recipes for future use.

Q6. Why is a recipe details page important?

It displays ingredients, cooking time and preparation instructions.

Q7. What is a user-friendly application?

An application that is simple, easy to understand and easy to use.

